 *
 * aen-power-stop overlay for the E1M-AEN801 (Ensemble E8, M55-HP), MRAM image.
 * BUILT, NOT BENCH-VERIFIED: the HE overlay beside it is the bench-proven one.
 *
 * The HP image must be MRAM-booted (VTOR >= 0x80000000): STOP wakes through a cold boot
 * and the HP has no TCM retention, so the backend refuses a TCM-booted HP image
 * (hp_vtor_not_mram).  Do NOT use the Flow C ITCM retarget for this app.
 *
 * Same pad controllers as the HE overlay: the SoM power layer drives the pads of every
 * present domain, and a pad whose GPIO controller is disabled makes the quiesce fail with
 * ALP_ERR_NOT_READY (RV-3028 INT on LPGPIO).  The stock board tree already enables
 * GPIO5 (backlight enable) and GPIO11 (PHY reset) and the LPGPIO bank; LPGPIO is
 * repeated so the overlay states everything the app needs.
 */
&lpgpio {
	status = "okay";
};
